WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.819 --> 00:00:05.750
The newest adaptation of Stephen King's It
has introduced yet another generation of kids

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:07.120
to their worst nightmares.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:12.320
The 1990 TV miniseries scared the jorts off
every early millennial with a VCR and four

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:13.320
hours to spare.

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:18.140
But the 2017 version moves the setting to
the late '80s, when milk cartons paraded pictures

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:22.550
of missing children, and the New Kids on the
Block were every teen's guiltiest Walkman

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:23.550
pleasure.

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:26.779
Through a wildly entertaining funhouse of
fright, the Losers Club comes together to

00:00:26.779 --> 00:00:29.550
do what the adults can't and banish evil.

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.699
But do they really put an end to their shared
enemy?

00:00:31.699 --> 00:00:35.360
Let's take a look at what actually happens
at the end of It.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:37.360
The Losers Club is strong...

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:41.180
There's an undercurrent of teenage rebellion
that informs the story of It.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:46.700
We have a group of misunderstood, underappreciated,
and in some cases even abused kids who, on

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:50.270
their own, are self-described Losers with
a capital L.

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:54.370
Bill Denbrough has a stutter and bears the
guilt of his little brother's disappearance.

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:59.290
Beverly Marsh has developed a wholly undeserved
reputation, just as her father asserts dominion

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:03.170
over her girlhood in creepy and possibly even
violent ways.

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:07.340
The delightfully foul-mouthed Richie Tozier
is content to spend every second of his spare

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:08.799
time in the arcade.

00:01:08.799 --> 00:01:13.520
Stanley Uris is constantly picked on for his
yarmulka, though he can barely recite Hebrew.

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:17.840
Mike Hanlon is the home-schooled kid who's
still considered "other" thanks to his race.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:21.530
Eddie Kaspbrak is whip-smart, but constantly
demeaned by his mother.

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:25.880
And Ben Hanscom is the new guy whose pudginess
and affinity for the library makes him an

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:28.550
easy mark for the nastiest of town bullies.

00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:33.000
By coming together, they ignite a uniquely
fearless and fun force field against the demonic

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.110
being that's plagued their town for years.

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:37.369
They're not invincible

00:01:37.369 --> 00:01:42.190
Unlike other kids, who are perhaps less subject
to daily torture by their peers, the Losers

00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:44.740
have been made to face their fears almost
daily.

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:48.409
From bullies to oppressive parents to lost
siblings, they've already been through the

00:01:48.409 --> 00:01:49.939
worst life can throw at them.

00:01:49.939 --> 00:01:54.240
So Pennywise, despite all its tricks, can
only do so much to them … especially when

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:55.240
they're united.

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:59.100
However, they do seem to have a tendency to
break apart a little too soon.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:04.040
As we see throughout the movie, Pennywise
constantly tries to separate them to individualize

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:06.540
the aggression, since he needs their fears
to feed.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.920
"Rich, what are you afraid of?"

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:13.020
"Clowns."

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:18.850
That scare tactic doesn't work so well when
they're together, but apart, they're completely

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:19.850
vulnerable.

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:23.180
At the end of the film, they agree to reunite
if the occasion calls, but they'll go their

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:27.580
separate ways in the meantime… which can't
be good news for the next victims.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:31.800
Standing alone, too, they're more likely to
backtrack in their own unique ways.

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:36.940
Book readers and fans of the miniseries will
know that Stan Uris isn't going to heal—inside

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:39.370
or out—quite as well as the others.

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:41.730
And as for Bevy, well …

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:43.670
Bev chooses herself… kind of

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:48.390
Apart from beating us over the head with metaphors
about her reaching adolescence, It also lays

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:51.730
on the love triangle element with Beverly
Marsh pretty thick.

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:56.420
Not counting her grotesque father, Beverly
is the apple of not one but two pairs of eyes:

00:02:56.420 --> 00:03:00.490
"January Embers" scribe Ben and the group's
de facto leader, Bill.

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:03.760
It's Ben's kiss that summons her from her
Pennywise-induced coma.

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:07.740
But it's Bill's lips she chooses to smooch
before her departure to her aunt's, now that

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:09.280
she's a self-made orphan.

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:12.720
But neither of these fellas are important
enough to keep her around Derry.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:17.180
Ben and Bill are just roadblocks to her retreat
from town… ones she happily bypasses, by

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:18.180
the way.

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:21.740
The bad news is that anyone familiar with
King's writing will know that her dad isn't

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:25.320
the only guy who'll hurt her before it's all
said and done.

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:27.400
Speaking of Mr. Marsh …

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:29.170
Parental plight

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:33.480
If you thought Disney movies had a heavy hand
with parents, It went hard on the moms and

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:34.940
dads of Derry, too.

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:37.390
Beverly greases her dad with a toilet lid.

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:40.840
Henry Bowers knifes his old man in the neck
just for making him look bad in front of his

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:41.840
friends.

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:44.400
And Mike Hanlon has lost his parents in a
horrific fire.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:47.390
Even the surviving parents are left a little
worse for wear.

00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:51.790
Bill has almost completely disregarded his
parents' sensitivities over their lost son,

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:55.440
and Eddie defies his mother's orders and trashes
his placebo prescriptions.

00:03:55.440 --> 00:04:00.380
Part of the point of this story is to subvert
the whole "parents know best" philosophy,

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:04.350
since, you know, they're largely ignoring
all the missing and murdered children around

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:05.350
town.

00:04:05.350 --> 00:04:09.210
It's basically a big metaphor for that moment
when kids realize their parents aren't perfect

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:12.600
and begin to think that they can take care
of themselves instead.

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:14.980
Henry Bowers is MIA

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:19.080
On top of Georgie and Henry's fire-spraying
henchman Patrick Hockstetter, the other minor

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:22.080
who seemingly meets his maker in the movie
is Henry Bowers.

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:26.510
After being coaxed into killing his old man
by visions of It, his sudden sense of social

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:30.110
supremacy takes over as he goes on the offensive
against Mike.

00:04:30.110 --> 00:04:34.320
Mike manages to fight him off and pitches
Henry into the abyss of Pennywise's well,

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:35.820
which is immeasurably deep.

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:37.950
But we shouldn't count Henry out just yet.

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:42.470
It's a well-known Hollywood rule that if a
character's death isn't shown on-screen, you're

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:44.650
better off assuming it didn't happen.

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:49.380
On top of that, in the story, Bowers plays
a bonkers part in future events.

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:54.500
So, his rage will likely linger just as long
as that terrible scar he sliced into Ben's

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:55.500
belly.

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:57.620
What about the floating kids?

00:04:57.620 --> 00:05:01.410
When Bill and the rest of the Losers come
back together to rescue Beverly from It, they

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:04.570
discover her floating mid-air with her eyes
glazed over.

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:06.000
"You'll float too!

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:07.430
You'll float too!

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:08.860
You'll float too!

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:10.300
You'll float too!"

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:14.060
After they spring her from unconsciousness,
they learn that she felt like she was no longer

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:16.370
alive while under the spell of the deadlights.

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:19.940
After the Losers manage to scare Pennywise
away, the rest of the kids that have been

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:22.600
floating in It's underground lair start to
drop.

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:24.400
Will they too emerge alive?

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:25.400
It's hard to tell.

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:29.690
Either way, though, it looks like little Georgie
won't be coming back to captain the SS Georgie

00:05:29.690 --> 00:05:31.430
again any time soon.

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:35.970
Although other lost children are potentially
being dropped to safety or at least absolution

00:05:35.970 --> 00:05:40.520
for their folks, Bill's left to grieve over
the yellow raincoat Georgie wore while captaining

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:42.250
his paper boat on the street.

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:46.500
Why he isn't in the floating kid cloud is
a bit of a mystery, so if you listen closely,

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:51.220
you can probably hear the Justice for Georgie
hashtag being formed right now.

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:52.340
It isn't over

00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:56.890
Although the Losers do manage to defeat It
at the end of the movie, even they know the

00:05:56.890 --> 00:05:57.910
fight isn't over.

00:05:57.910 --> 00:06:02.050
We get a glimpse of It falling apart, but
the creature clearly isn't dead.

00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:06.800
As the news articles Ben has so carefully
assembled indicate, It's hunger strikes again

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:08.000
every few decades.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:13.070
So, it's just a matter of time before It comes
back to claim another slew of victims in Chapter

00:06:13.070 --> 00:06:14.070
Two.

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:17.380
And when it does, everyone in the Losers Club
will reunite in Derry to finish what they

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:20.260
started -- almost all of them at least.

00:06:20.260 --> 00:06:21.260
Thanks for watching!

00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:23.530
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:25.520
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

